    <div class="atw-faq-grid">

      <div class="atw-faq-item" data-reveal="scale">

        <h3>
          What does the Full Package include?
        </h3>

        <p>
          Full Package combines complete Interior Detailing and Exterior Detailing
          in one appointment, including carpet & fabric shampoo/agitation and exterior paint sealant.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="atw-faq-item" data-reveal="scale">

        <h3>
          What is the difference between Full Package and Restore Package?
        </h3>

        <p>
          Restore includes everything in the Full Package plus a one-step machine polish
          to improve gloss, clarity and light surface defects.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="atw-faq-item" data-reveal="scale">

        <h3>
          Is seat extraction included?
        </h3>

        <p>
          Carpet & fabric shampoo/agitation is included as needed. Deeper Seat Extraction is an optional upgrade:
          +$100 for Standard vehicles and +$175 for Large vehicles. Van or oversized configurations require a quote.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="atw-faq-item" data-reveal="scale">

        <h3>
          Is pet hair removal included?
        </h3>

        <p>
          Light pet hair is included. Moderate pet hair is +$30, heavy is +$50,
          and extreme cases require a custom quote.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="atw-faq-item" data-reveal="scale">

        <h3>
          Does Full Package include machine polishing?
        </h3>

        <p>
          No. Machine polishing is not part of the Full Package.
          Choose Restore Package if you want Full Detailing plus a one-step machine polish.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="atw-faq-item" data-reveal="scale">

        <h3>
          Do I need to bring my vehicle to a shop?
        </h3>

        <p>
          No. ATW Detailing is mobile. We come to your home,
          workplace or another suitable location within our service area.
        </p>

